.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt FAND.CPROFILE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fand.cprofile
.Nd Cooling profile file format
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A cooling profile is a list of temperature steps with their corresponding target
duty cycle.
The steps must be in ascending temperature order.
Temperatures must be expressed consistently with the temperature sensor read by
.Pa fand ,
i.e., both the
.Fl K
and
.Fl m
options apply to them.
The profile is read from a file in
.Xr libucl 3
format with the following properties:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa lo_duty
The duty cycle, expressed in nanoseconds, to use when temperature is lower than
the first temperature step.
.It
.Pa steps
A list of at most 10 temperature steps in ascending order.
The name of the step is arbitrary.
Each step must have the following properties:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa temp
The step's low boundary temperature.
Its high boundary temperature, if any, is its next step's
.Pa temp
property.
.It
.Pa duty
The step's duty cycle, expressed in nanoseconds.
.El
.El
When a cooling profile is used,
.Pa fand
will keep the PWM enabled until it exit.
This is in contrast with manual configuration where the
.Fl o
option will disable it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Here is a sample cooling profile assuming neither the
.Fl K
nor the
.Fl m
options are
used:
.Bd -literal
lo_duty = 532;   # nanoseconds, 1%
steps {
    #          °C           nanoseconds
    0 { temp = 25.0; duty =   532; } #  1%
    1 { temp = 30.0; duty = 10649; } # 20%
    2 { temp = 35.0; duty = 25026; } # 47%
    3 { temp = 40.0; duty = 41533; } # 78%
    4 { temp = 45.0; duty = 52183; } # 98%
}
.Ed
This sample cooling profile will set duty cycle to:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
532 ns when under 25 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa lo_duty
.It
532 ns when between 25 and 29 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa steps 0
.It
10649 ns when between 30 and 34 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa steps 1
.It
25026 ns when between 35 and 39 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa steps 2
.It
41533 ns when between 40 and 44 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa steps 3
.It
and 52183 ns when above 45 degrees Celsius, honoring
.Pa steps 4
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libucl 3 ,
.Xr fand 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
This manual page were originally written by
.An Stéphane Rochoy Aq Mt sheda@FreeBSD.org .
.Sh BUGS
Cooling profile lake support for:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
setting the PWM period
.It
enabling polarity inversion
.It
setting the temperature unit
.It
setting the temperature multiplier
.El
And the number of temperature steps is limited to 10.
